<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Beatrix of the Netherlands</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">born 1938</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Queen Beatrix</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Beatrix was Queen of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-the-netherlands">Netherlands</a> from 1980 to 2013, succeeding her mother Juliana. Her marriage to the German diplomat Claus von Amsberg in 1966 provoked protests, but she became a respected and active head of state who took a close interest in government. She abdicated on 30 April 2013 in favour of her son Willem-Alexander.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/beatrix-of-the-netherlands.jpg" alt="Beatrix of the Netherlands" width="320" height="453" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: RVD Koninklijk Huis · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Prinses_Beatrix.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
